Bounds -- an option for the function fpt specifying lower and upper bounds for the F-pure threshold
***************************************************************************************************

Description
===========

An option for the function *note fpt: fpt, specifying bounds for the $F$-pure
threshold. Bounds accepts lists consisting of two numbers, namely a lower and
an upper bound for the $F$-pure threshold being computed. This useful feature
allows the user to refine bounds obtained in previous computations, as
illustrated below.

+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/5[x,y];                                         |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : f = x^7*y^5*(x + y)^5*(x^2 + y^3)^4;                   |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : fpt(f, DepthOfSearch => 3, Attempts => 5)              |
|                                                            |
|       19   1                                               |
|o3 = {---, --}                                              |
|      250  13                                               |
|                                                            |
|o3 : List                                                   |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : fpt(f, DepthOfSearch => 3, Attempts => 5, Bounds => oo)|
|                                                            |
|       45   1                                               |
|o4 = {---, --}                                              |
|      589  13                                               |
|                                                            |
|o4 : List                                                   |
+------------------------------------------------------------+

Functions with optional argument named Bounds:
==============================================

  * "fpt(...,Bounds=>...)" -- see *note fpt: fpt, -- attempt to compute the
    F-pure threshold of a polynomial at the origin or globally

