ContainmentTest -- an option for the function frobeniusNu specifying the type of containment of powers of ideals to test
************************************************************************************************************************

Description
===========

An option for the function *note frobeniusNu: frobeniusNu, specifying which
type of containment test to apply. The valid values are StandardPower,
FrobeniusRoot, GlobalFrobeniusRoot, FrobeniusPower, and null. When the option
*note AtOrigin: (TestIdeals)AtOrigin, is set to true, the default value for
ContainmentTest, null, is replaced with FrobeniusRoot when the second argument
passed to *note frobeniusNu: frobeniusNu, is a ring element, and StandardPower
when that argument is an ideal. When *note AtOrigin: (TestIdeals)AtOrigin, is
set to false, the value GlobalFrobeniusRoot is used.

Functions with optional argument named ContainmentTest:
=======================================================

  * "frobeniusNu(...,ContainmentTest=>...)" -- see *note frobeniusNu:
    frobeniusNu, -- computes the largest power of an ideal not contained in a
    specified Frobenius power

