UseSpecialAlgorithms -- an option for the functions fpt and frobeniusNu to use special algorithms to speed up computations
**************************************************************************************************************************

Description
===========

An option for the functions *note fpt: fpt, and *note frobeniusNu:
frobeniusNu,. Takes on Boolean values; default value is true, in both
functions.

If this option is set to true in *note fpt: fpt,, that function checks whether
the input is a diagonal polynomial, a binomial, a product of factors in simple
normal crossing, or a form in two variables, in which case specialized
algorithms or formulas are used.

If set to true in *note frobeniusNu: frobeniusNu,, that function checks whether
the input is one of the above special types of polynomials, in which case it
computes the $F$-pure threshold of the polynomial, and uses the $F$-pure
threshold to compute the nu invariant.

Functions with optional argument named UseSpecialAlgorithms:
============================================================

  * "fpt(...,UseSpecialAlgorithms=>...)" -- see *note fpt: fpt, -- attempt to
    compute the F-pure threshold of a polynomial at the origin or globally
  * "frobeniusNu(...,UseSpecialAlgorithms=>...)" -- see *note frobeniusNu:
    frobeniusNu, -- computes the largest power of an ideal not contained in a
    specified Frobenius power

For the programmer
==================

The object *note UseSpecialAlgorithms: UseSpecialAlgorithms, is a *note symbol:
